BetterString.mcc/BetterString.mcc

    NAME
        BetterString.mcc -- Single-line text editing with selection and
        actions.

    SUPERCLASS
        Area.mui

    DESCRIPTION
        Provide an editable byte string with dynamic storage, selection,
        clipboard operations, and filename completion. This AROS source
        defines version 11.33. BetterString derives from Area, not String; it
        implements selected MUIA_String attributes itself. Positions and
        lengths refer to bytes, not Unicode characters.
        Use the normal MUI Application, Window, and Area lifecycle. Editing
        and actions run synchronously in the calling task. Clipboard
        operations wait for a server reply; completion locks and enumerates
        DOS directories or DOS-list entries. No operation timeout is exposed
        by this class.
        MUIA_String_Contents copies supplied text; NULL clears it. Get returns
        borrowed internal storage, which editing or reallocation can
        invalidate. Never free or modify that storage. Keep borrowed
        Accept/Reject strings, EditHook, popup/list/focus objects, and
        InactiveContents valid while configured. The class does not take
        ownership of those inputs.

    NOTES
        The initial content buffer is empty; construction processes supplied
        attributes and then resets BufferPos to zero. MaxLen defaults to zero
        (no configured limit). A nonzero MaxLen includes the terminator.
        Several length and position fields are 16-bit; zero does not promise
        unlimited representable text. Use bounded application inputs.
        The setter can change caller tag IDs to TAG_IGNORE, including
        redundant or suppressed Contents tags and Integer tags. Use writable
        tag storage. Setting Contents does not create a general undo history.
        Redraw requests and contents notifications are separate; action
        success is not proof that the content changed.
        NoInput and NoShortcuts affect particular input paths; neither is an
        access-control boundary. Programmatic edits and standard MUI key
        actions have separate handling. Secret suppresses clipboard copying,
        but display masking depends on successful temporary allocation. It is
        not a reliable confidentiality guarantee under allocation failure.
        Contents remains readable and no explicit memory-wiping guarantee is
        provided.

    BUGS
        The Revert snapshot taken on activation uses an incorrect copy length
        and can be incomplete. Revert is not a reliable exact restoration
        operation in this source. HexToDec also has an incorrect accumulation
        expression and must not be relied on for multi-digit conversion.
        Allocation and completion failures are not uniformly propagated. The
        method-specific entries describe the observable result rather than
        promising transactional edits or complete error reporting.

    COPYRIGHT
        Copyright (C) 2005-2018 BetterString.mcc Open Source Team
        $Id$
        Distributed under the GNU Lesser General Public License. Third-party
        copyright is retained.
BetterString.mcc/MUIA_BetterString_Columns

    NAME
        MUIA_BetterString_Columns

    FUNCTION
        Set the width used when calculating layout.

    INPUTS
        Initialize, set; ULONG, stored as UWORD. Default zero.

    NOTES
        A nonzero value contributes Columns times the current font width of n
        to minimum, default, and maximum width. It is not a content-length
        limit. Zero uses flexible width contributions of 10, 100, and
        MBQ_MUI_MAXMAX. OM_SET also stores this value but does not request relayout;
        supply it at construction for initial layout. No local getter exists.
BetterString.mcc/MUIA_BetterString_InactiveContents

    NAME
        MUIA_BetterString_InactiveContents

    FUNCTION
        Display placeholder text while the object is inactive and its content
        is empty.

    INPUTS
        Initialize, set, get; STRPTR. Default NULL.

    NOTES
        The pointer is borrowed, not copied. Keep the NUL-terminated string
        valid until replacement or disposal; Get returns the same read-only
        borrowed pointer. It does not become String_Contents. Set requests
        redraw. Rendering uses a reduced-intensity color on true-color
        displays; the other path requests italic style and a shadow pen.
        Italic rendering is not universal.
BetterString.mcc/MUIA_BetterString_KeyUpFocus

    NAME
        MUIA_BetterString_KeyUpFocus

    FUNCTION
        Move active focus on the UP MUI key.

    INPUTS
        Initialize, set, get; Object *. Default NULL.

    NOTES
        When the target and current window exist, set Window_ActiveObject to
        the target and consume the event. This changes Window_ActiveObject, not Window_DefaultObject. The pointer is
        borrowed: keep the target alive and appropriate for the same window.
        NULL leaves that handling to other input paths. Get returns the
        configured pointer.
BetterString.mcc/MUIA_BetterString_KeyDownFocus

    NAME
        MUIA_BetterString_KeyDownFocus

    FUNCTION
        Move active focus on the DOWN MUI key.

    INPUTS
        Initialize, set, get; Object *. Default NULL.

    NOTES
        When the target and current window exist, set Window_ActiveObject to
        the target and consume the event. This changes Window_ActiveObject, not Window_DefaultObject. The pointer is
        borrowed: keep the target alive and appropriate for the same window.
        NULL leaves that handling to other input paths. Get returns the
        configured pointer.
BetterString.mcc/MUIA_BetterString_NoInput

    NAME
        MUIA_BetterString_NoInput

    FUNCTION
        Restrict ordinary raw-key editing.

    INPUTS
        Initialize, set, get; BOOL. Default FALSE.

    NOTES
        TRUE blocks typed-character insertion and raw-key Tab completion,
        Backspace, and Delete, while allowing navigation, selection, copying,
        and acknowledgement. It is not a comprehensive read-only mode:
        standard MUI key actions are handled before this check, and Contents,
        Insert, and DoAction do not consult it. Setting it alone does not
        request redraw.
BetterString.mcc/MUIA_BetterString_NoNotify

    NAME
        MUIA_BetterString_NoNotify

    FUNCTION
        Defer BetterString contents notifications.

    INPUTS
        Initialize, set, get; BOOL. Default FALSE.

    NOTES
        TRUE queues a pending-notification flag instead of forwarding
        notifications from TriggerNotify. Contents setting also suppresses its
        tag when a change would notify. When the flag is cleared and a
        notification is pending, the class forwards one String_Contents
        notification with current content and clears the pending flag.
        Repeated changes are coalesced, not recorded individually. This
        affects contents notification paths, not all attributes or
        String_Acknowledge. It is distinct from MUIA_NoNotify. Keep batched
        changes and the final reset in separate calls when notification
        ordering matters.
BetterString.mcc/MUIA_BetterString_NoShortcuts

    NAME
        MUIA_BetterString_NoShortcuts

    FUNCTION
        Disable the built-in raw-key command shortcuts.

    INPUTS
        Initialize, set, get; BOOL. Default FALSE.

    NOTES
        TRUE disables these shortcuts; FALSE enables them. Standard
        MUIKEY_COPY/CUT/PASTE/UNDO/REDO handling remains available, as do
        navigation and direct DoAction calls.
        With shortcuts enabled, the command-key actions include c/x/v for
        copy/cut/paste, z/Z for undo/redo, q for revert, g/G for case
        conversion, i/d for number adjustment, #/$ for hexadecimal/decimal
        conversion, and right-command Tab (Shift for reverse) for completion.
        The action limitations also apply to shortcuts.
        Raw-key navigation uses Shift-Left/Right for line start/end and
        Alt-Left/Right for previous/next word. Control with cursor movement
        extends a selection. Shift or Control with Backspace deletes toward
        the start; with Delete it deletes toward the end. Alt-Backspace/Delete
        deletes toward the previous/next word. Home and End also move to the
        respective line boundary.
BetterString.mcc/MUIA_BetterString_SelectOnActive

    NAME
        MUIA_BetterString_SelectOnActive

    FUNCTION
        Control selecting all content when the object becomes active.

    INPUTS
        Initialize, set, get; BOOL. Without an explicit override, use the user
        preference (compiled default FALSE).

    NOTES
        Keyboard/application activation selects immediately; mouse activation
        cooperates with click/drag selection and mouse-button release. FALSE
        forces selection off; TRUE forces it on. No public value restores the
        unspecified preference state. Get reports the effective flag
        combination. Setup manages a Window_Sleep notification through a
        private attribute, so sleeping/waking can change the effective
        override. Prefer the user preference unless the application requires
        different behavior.
BetterString.mcc/MUIA_BetterString_SelectSize

    NAME
        MUIA_BetterString_SelectSize

    FUNCTION
        Set or read the signed selection length.

    INPUTS
        Initialize, set, get in this implementation; LONG. Default zero.

    NOTES
        Set anchors the selection at the current BufferPos and places the
        other endpoint at BufferPos plus the supplied value, clamped to the
        content bounds. Positive extends right, negative left. Get returns
        endpoint minus anchor when selection is enabled, otherwise zero. Zero
        has no visible selected span. Set requests redraw. BufferPos changes
        clear selection; tag order therefore matters. Construction accepts
        this tag but later resets BufferPos to zero.
BetterString.mcc/MUIA_BetterString_StayActive

    NAME
        MUIA_BetterString_StayActive

    FUNCTION
        Suppress this handler's normal deactivation on Return and an outside
        click.

    INPUTS
        Initialize, set, get; BOOL. Default FALSE.

    NOTES
        Return still sends String_Acknowledge. When FALSE, Return advances to
        the next/previous object if String_AdvanceOnCR is set, otherwise
        clears the active object. TRUE skips that focus change. This does not
        prevent explicit focus changes by the application, Window, or other
        controls. No local redraw is requested merely by setting the flag.
BetterString.mcc/MUIM_BetterString_ClearSelected

    NAME
        MUIM_BetterString_ClearSelected

    SYNOPSIS
        IPTR result = DoMethod(obj, MUIM_BetterString_ClearSelected);

    FUNCTION
        Delete the selected span through DoAction(Delete).

    INPUTS
        obj - Live BetterString object. No payload arguments.

    RESULT
        Always TRUE after dispatching the action; the delegated result is
        ignored.

    NOTES
        Without a nonempty selection, no character is deleted. The action
        still saves an undo snapshot, clears selection, requests redraw, and
        triggers or queues a contents notification. NoInput is not checked.
        This is not the raw Delete key, which can delete the character at the
        cursor.
BetterString.mcc/MUIM_BetterString_DoAction

    NAME
        MUIM_BetterString_DoAction

    SYNOPSIS
        IPTR result = DoMethod(obj, MUIM_BetterString_DoAction, action);

    FUNCTION
        Perform a selection, editing, clipboard, or completion action.

    INPUTS
        action - One MUIV_BetterString_DoAction_* constant from the public
        enumeration.
        obj - Live BetterString in the normal GUI lifecycle. Revert requires
        an available activation snapshot; completion requires valid DOS-path
        content.

    RESULT
        Action-dependent TRUE/FALSE. Unknown action values return FALSE. TRUE
        does not consistently mean that data changed or all underlying
        operations succeeded.

    NOTES
        Cut (1): with a selected span, attempt to copy it and delete it;
        without a selection, clear the entire string without copying it to the
        clipboard. Return TRUE.
        Copy (2): copy the selected span or the whole string when unselected,
        then clear selection. Secret content is not copied. Return TRUE even
        when copying is suppressed or fails.
        Paste (3): read the clipboard, delete a selected span, and insert at
        the cursor. MaxLen can truncate and beep. Accept/Reject are not
        applied. Return TRUE even if reading or allocation fails; selection is
        cleared. There is no rollback of a selection deleted before a later
        failure.
        SelectAll (4) and SelectNone (5): enable a full-content selection or
        clear selection. Return TRUE without a contents notification.
        Undo (6) and Redo (7): swap one saved content buffer and cursor
        position when that direction is available; otherwise return FALSE.
        This is one alternating undo/redo slot, not a complete edit history.
        Revert (8): swap current content with the activation snapshot, clear
        selection, and put the cursor at the end. Return TRUE. The snapshot
        must exist; the incorrect activation copy length means exact
        restoration is not guaranteed.
        ToggleCase (9): change case at the cursor and advance one byte; return
        FALSE at the terminator. ToggleCaseWord (10): change case through the
        start of the next word, advancing the cursor; return FALSE if nothing
        is traversed. Locale character functions operate on bytes.
        IncreaseNum (11) and DecreaseNum (12): find a digit run at the cursor,
        then to its right, then to its left; parse it and adjust an unsigned
        value, preserving minimum field width. Decrement returns FALSE for
        zero. These are not arbitrary-precision operations; replacement
        failure is not propagated reliably.
        HexToDec (13): intended to replace the hexadecimal run around the
        cursor with decimal text. The accumulation is defective in this
        source; do not rely on numeric correctness. DecToHex (14): locate a
        decimal run and replace it with lowercase hexadecimal text. Both
        return FALSE when no applicable run is found; TRUE does not verify the
        replacement.
        NextFileComp (15) and PrevFileComp (16): perform synchronous DOS
        completion, cycling cached directory matches forward/backward. The
        first directory match is chosen by direction. Volume completion picks
        the first matching DOS-list entry rather than cycling a result list.
        Completion uses bounded legacy filename buffers and does not guarantee
        full long-name preservation. FALSE means no reported edit; failure
        does not imply an unchanged buffer or fully cleared completion state.
        Delete (17): remove only a nonempty selected span and clear selection.
        Return TRUE even when nothing was selected. This differs from pressing
        the Delete key.
        All actions request redraw, including unknown ones. Actions marked as
        edits trigger or queue Contents notifications, sometimes even when
        text did not change. Copy and selection-only actions do not. NoInput
        and NoShortcuts are not checked by this method.

    SEE ALSO
        MUIA_BetterString_NoNotify, MUIA_BetterString_NoShortcuts
BetterString.mcc/MUIM_BetterString_FileNameStart

    NAME
        MUIM_BetterString_FileNameStart

    SYNOPSIS
        LONG start = (LONG)DoMethod(obj, MUIM_BetterString_FileNameStart,
        (IPTR)buffer, pos);

    FUNCTION
        Locate the start of a DOS path for filename completion.

    INPUTS
        buffer - Readable NUL-terminated byte string.
        pos - LONG offset from zero through the string length. The method does
        not modify or retain buffer.

    RESULT
        The beginning of the path containing the colon found at or before pos,
        or MUIR_BetterString_FileNameStart_Volume (-1) if no colon is found.

    NOTES
        Scan backward for a colon. If found, scan farther back to a double
        quote, greater-than sign, space, equals sign, or the start of the
        string. This is a simple delimiter scan, not a general URL or shell
        parser. Completion calls this method through dispatch, allowing a
        subclass to override it. An override must return a valid path-start
        offset for the caller's DOS-path handling or the volume sentinel; it
        must not return an unrelated index.
BetterString.mcc/MUIM_BetterString_Insert

    NAME
        MUIM_BetterString_Insert

    SYNOPSIS
        IPTR result = DoMethod(obj, MUIM_BetterString_Insert, (IPTR)text,
        pos);

    FUNCTION
        Insert text at a specified byte position.

    INPUTS
        text - Non-NULL readable NUL-terminated string, independent of the
        internal content buffer.
        pos - LONG byte offset within the current content, including its end;
        or MUIV_BetterString_Insert_StartOfString (0), EndOfString (-2), or
        BufferPos (-1). Use the full constant names from the public header.

    RESULT
        Always TRUE after calling the overwrite helper. Its truncation result
        is not propagated.

    NOTES
        The helper copies the text and shifts following bytes. It moves
        BufferPos when the cursor is at or after the insertion point. MaxLen
        can truncate insertion and cause DisplayBeep. The method clears
        selection without replacing its span, requests redraw, and triggers or
        queues a Contents notification. It does not check NoInput or
        Accept/Reject and does not save an undo snapshot. Supply valid
        offsets; arbitrary out-of-range positions are not clamped. Allocation
        failure is not handled as an atomic failed edit.

